  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining App Structure**\n\nI\'ve started sketching out the app\'s foundational components, particularly the data persistence layer. I\'m focusing on defining the `FocusSessionEntity` within the `com.example.data` package, meticulously recording session details like start time, duration, session type (deep focus or mind pause), completion status, and the targeted app.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Entities**\n\nI\'m now expanding the data entities, specifically `BlockedAttemptEntity` and `GuardedAppEntity`. I\'m meticulously designing how to record blocked attempts, including details like package names, timestamps, the blocked feature, and the action taken. I\'m also structuring the `GuardedAppEntity` to track guarded apps, their configuration, daily limits, and mindful pause durations. The focus is now on the DAO and database interactions to ensure efficient data management.\n\n\n**Developing UI Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the accessibility service with the UI via the ViewModel. My current focus is on detecting \"Reels\" nodes using a `NodeInfo` hierarchy and triggering either a back action, a system alert, or the MindfulOverlayActivity based on the `isReelsBlockEnabled` flag. The accessibility service config is being set up to define accessibility flags and feedback types, with all state being exposed via the `FocusViewModel`.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now creating the UI components and screens, focusing on `com.example.ui`. I\'m going with a modern slate dark theme, `#0F172A`, accented by emerald/teal and warm coral. The dashboard will feature a service status banner, focus stats, and an anti-doomscroll vulnerability meter. I will be incorporating a \"Test Reels Block Overlay\" button for immediate user experience testing. The Guarded Apps screen will list social apps with block switches.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 16059054
    }
