    modified_response: "I have built **FocusGuard - Reel Detox & Screen Time**, an Android application designed to help users battle phone addiction, stop doomscrolling on social media (specifically targeting short-form video feeds like Instagram Reels, TikTok, and YouTube Shorts), and reclaim focus.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n\n- **Android Accessibility Anti-Doomscroll Engine**:\n  - `FocusGuardAccessibilityService`: Leverages standard Android Accessibility APIs to detect when short-form video feeds (such as Instagram Reels or TikTok) are opened in the foreground.\n  - Automatically issues a back gesture or displays a **Mindfulness Pause Overlay** when a Reel/Shorts trigger is detected.\n- **Interactive Simulation & Testing**:\n  - A **\"Simulate Instagram Reels Block\"** action on the Dashboard allowing users to preview the exact mindfulness pause popup and log simulated intercepts directly inside the app.\n- **App Distraction Guard Controls**:\n  - Per-app customization for Instagram, TikTok, YouTube Shorts, X/Twitter, and Reddit.\n  - Toggle switches for **Auto-Block Reels & Shorts**, **Mindful Pause Overlays**, and customizable **Daily Screen Time Limits** (5 to 60 minutes).\n- **Mindful Focus & Breathing Timer**:\n  - Pomodoro/Deep Focus timer with an animated breathing guide ring (Inhale/Exhale rhythm) and preset chips (10m, 25m, 45m).\n- **Local Room Persistence**:\n  - Room Database (`AppDatabase`, `FocusDao`, `FocusRepository`) storing guarded app settings, recent intercept logs with timestamps, and calculated saved minutes.\n- **Design & Adaptive Theme**:\n  - Custom **FocusGuardTheme** with a dark slate canvas and teal/emerald accents.\n  - Full support for Material 3 design, edge-to-edge window insets, bottom navigation, and custom launcher adaptive icon."
