    thinking: "**Analyzing Instagram Bug**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause of Instagram\'s back-gesture issue: `FocusGuardAccessibilityService.kt`. The culprit is line 122, where `performGlobalAction(GLOBAL_ACTION_BACK)` is triggered immediately upon detecting nodes matching \"reels\" or \"reel.\" This is happening without any delay. The current implementation is too aggressive, and is back-gesturing before the user even has a chance to see the page.\n\n\n**Refining Bug Fix Logic**\n\nI\'ve determined the issue\'s persistence is tied to Instagram\'s persistent \"Reels\" tab, even on the main feed. My revised approach incorporates a 3-second throttle on the back gesture, preventing the aggressive trigger. This resolves the initial rapid back-gesture on launch. My analysis of the user\'s feedback guides the implementation\'s direction: it needs to be more robust. Now, I will design a new implementation to address the user\'s specific preferences.\n\n\n**Designing Improved Reel Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focused on a nuanced approach. The initial fix was good, but I need to ensure the back gesture isn\'t triggered from the main feed tab bar. I\'m looking at checking for active Reels video viewer class names, instead of the main tab icon, to determine if it is appropriate. I\'m also exploring a \"Mindfulness Nudge\" by implementing a timed Reels usage check. This will alert users to their usage with an overlay after a configurable duration.\n\n\n**Implementing User Control Options**\n\nI\'m now integrating user-configurable options within the app\'s settings. I\'ll include an enforcement action selector for a \"Mindfulness Overlay Pop-up\" (recommended) versus an \"Auto-Back Gesture\" (with a 30-second cooldown). Additionally, sliders will allow users to customize Reels time limits before pop-ups appear. I\'m also including a switch for the \"Main Feed Mindfulness Nudge\" to enable or disable it. The goal is complete user control.\n\n\n**Adding Setup Guide Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating a detailed setup guide within `SetupGuideScreen`. The guide clarifies Android accessibility and window overlay operations, emphasizing sandbox security and non-intrusive mindfulness prompts. I am updating the data model, repository, database, service, viewmodel, and UI components as required. I have inspected `Entities.kt` and updated `GuardedApp` fields.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 113664810
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
