  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Applet Completion**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the initial applet compilation was successful. Now, I\'m shifting focus to remaining requirements and user feedback, specifically regarding a reported Instagram issue: the app repeatedly executing back gestures on launch. I need to understand this problem\'s scope and verify that the intended user experience aligns with the final build.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have updated FocusGuard to resolve the repeated back-gesture issue and introduced the requested timed mindfulness pop-ups:\n\n- **Eliminated Back-Gesture Loop**: Removed the automatic back gesture on app launch. FocusGuard now accurately differentiates between active full-screen Reels viewing and general app navigation, eliminating repeated gestures and keeping Instagram completely usable.\n- **Timed Reels Mindfulness Pop-Up**: Configured timed monitoring for Reels. After watching Reels continuously for a customizable duration (e.g., 30 seconds), a non-intrusive mindfulness overlay appears inviting you to pause or return home.\n- **Main Feed Mindfulness Pop-Up**: Added an option in App Distraction Guards to enable timed mindfulness reminders on the main scrolling feed after a configurable scroll duration (e.g., 3 minutes).\n- **Customizable Enforcement Modes**: In the App Settings card, you can switch between **Mindfulness Pop-Up Overlay** (recommended, non-intrusive) and **Smart Back Gesture** (equipped with a 30-second safety cooldown to prevent repeating loops).\n- **Updated Setup & Architecture Guide**: Added clear explanations in the Setup Guide detailing how Android Accessibility and System Window Overlays provide safe, private, on-device digital wellbeing without modifying third-party binaries."
