  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Fixes**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the compilation\'s success and am now meticulously reviewing the changes to address the back gesture issue and the crash. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the root cause and implemented solution for the crash, which involved newly added fields within the `@` structure. I\'m keen on verifying all implemented fixes are sound.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have fixed the issue causing the launch crash and made the Instagram Reels detox functionality much more flexible and robust:\n\n### 1. Fixed App Launch Crash\n- **Database Schema Migration**: Updated Room database to **Version 2**. When new configuration fields were added to the app settings entity without incrementing the database version, Room encountered a schema mismatch on launch. Incrementing the version triggers clean migration and table generation on startup.\n- **Overlay Permission Guard**: Added a runtime check for `Settings.canDrawOverlays()` before attempting to render system pop-ups, preventing `BadTokenException` crashes if the \"Display Over Other Apps\" permission isn\'t granted.\n- **Persistent State**: Ensured existing app preferences are preserved across app launches rather than re-initialized.\n\n### 2. Improved Intercept Logic (No More Repeated Back Gestures)\n- **Mindfulness Pop-Up Mode (Default)**: Instead of abruptly triggering repeated back gestures that break app navigation, FocusGuard now presents a clean, non-intrusive mindfulness overlay prompting you to take a breath or return home.\n- **Action Cooldown**: Smart back gestures (if enabled) now enforce a minimum 30-second action cooldown to prevent loops.\n- **Custom Reels Time Limit**: Set a custom watch timer threshold (e.g., 10s to 180s continuous Reels scrolling) before the prompt triggers.\n- **Main Feed Mindfulness Option**: Toggle optional mindfulness pop-ups on the main feed after a configurable scroll duration (e.g., 3 minutes).\n- **Setup Guide**: Added quick shortcut button to grant the optional \"Display Over Other Apps\" permission in Android Settings."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 829874718
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
